.TH GRIDOT 1 "2026-10-06" "gridot 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gridot \- get rid of that: report unused packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gridot
.RI [ scan ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B gridot track
.I name
.I pkg
.RI [ pkg ...]
.br
.B gridot untrack
.I name
.br
.B gridot groups
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gridot
reads dpkg/apt or dnf/yum/rpm package state, builds the dependency graph, and reports
packages that nothing depends on any more. It never installs or removes anything.
.PP
A package is reported as an orphan when it is installed, was auto-installed, is not
essential or protected (on apt: not
.I required
or
.I important
priority; on dnf: not
.BR dnf ,
a kernel or a
.I protected.d
package), is not a member of a tracked group, and is not kept alive by an edge from
another installed package. On apt the edges are
.BR Pre-Depends ,
.B Depends
and (unless
.BR \-\-no\-recommends )
.BR Recommends ;
on dnf/yum they are
.BR Requires ,
.B Recommends
(unless
.BR \-\-no\-recommends )
and file-based requires such as
.IR /usr/bin/gpg2 .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Report orphaned packages grouped by dpkg section. This is the default command.
.TP
.BI track " name" " pkg" ...
Create a tracked group called
.I name
containing
.IR pkg .
Use
.B \-g
to add packages to an existing group instead.
.TP
.BI untrack " name"
Stop tracking the group called
.IR name .
.TP
.B groups
List tracked groups and their status.
.SH SCAN OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-min\-size " MiB"
Only report orphans at least this large, in MiB.
.TP
.BI \-n ", " \-\-limit " N"
Show at most
.I N
orphans in the detail list.
.TP
.BI \-r ", " \-\-root " pkg"
Treat
.I pkg
as a manual root even if it was auto-installed. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-groups
Skip the tracked-groups section.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-recommends
Ignore
.B Recommends
edges. This over-reports, because apt and dnf install recommended packages by default.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error, e.g. dpkg state unavailable or an unreadable group store.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gridot/groups.tsv
Tracked-group store, unless
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
overrides the base directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B gridot scan \-\-min\-size 20 \-\-limit 10
Report the ten largest orphans of at least 20 MiB.
.TP
.B gridot track audio pulseaudio pipewire
Track a use case so its parts are reported as AT RISK instead of orphan.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dpkg (1),
.BR apt (8),
.BR apt-mark (8),
.BR rpm (8),
.BR dnf (8),
.BR yum (8),
.BR deborphan (1),
.BR aptitude (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/codersilicon/gridot/issues
